# Card Shop
# A pack is bought and opened in one call: the response carries the five cards, and they are filed in the
# player's collection (PlayerCards) at the same time. Price, size and odds come from the backend so the shop
# page can never disagree with what a purchase actually does.

# Environment Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5041
@shopPath = /api/shop
@contentType = application/json
@accept = application/json

### The pack on offer: price, card count and the odds of every card level
# 1,500 coins for 5 cards. Level odds are (600 - 20x) / 49 percent for x = 1..10, i.e. 11.84 % at level 1
# down to 8.16 % at level 10, and a card of the drawn level is then picked uniformly.
GET {{baseUrl}}{{shopPath}}/pack
Accept: {{accept}}
{{authHeader}}

###

### Buy (and open) a pack
# 200 -> { success, price, coinsAfter, cards: [ { id, name, image, level, …, quantityOwned, isNew } ] }.
# Every card is drawn independently, so the same card can appear twice in one pack, and a card the player
# already owns simply raises its quantity (`isNew: false`).
POST {{baseUrl}}{{shopPath}}/pack/purchase
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{accept}}
{{authHeader}}

{}

###

### Not enough coins -> 400 (nothing is written: no coins spent, no cards filed)
POST {{baseUrl}}{{shopPath}}/pack/purchase
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{accept}}
{{authHeader}}

{}

###

### No token -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}{{shopPath}}/pack
Accept: {{accept}}

###

### The collection itself (endpoint only — there is no "My Cards" screen yet)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/player/cards
Accept: {{accept}}
{{authHeader}}

###
